-- VIVA QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS (HINGLISH)
-- =========================================

-- Q1. What is a trigger in PL/SQL?
-- Ans: Trigger ek stored PL/SQL block hai jo
-- specified database event par automatically execute hota hai.

-- Q2. What is the purpose of EMP_DELETE_AUDIT?
-- Ans: Is table mein delete kiye gaye employees ki
-- details aur deletion date store hoti hai.

-- Q3. What does BEFORE DELETE mean?
-- Ans: Employee record delete hone se pehle trigger execute hota hai.

-- Q4. What is :OLD?
-- Ans: :OLD deleted hone wali employee row ki
-- existing values access karne ke liye use hota hai.

-- Q5. Why is FOR EACH ROW used?
-- Ans: Isse trigger har deleted employee row ke liye execute hota hai.

-- Q6. What is SYSDATE?
-- Ans: SYSDATE database server ki current date aur time return karta hai.

-- Q7. Does the trigger need to be called manually?
-- Ans: Nahi, DELETE statement execute hone par trigger automatically fire hota hai.

-- Q8. Why do we store deleted employee information?
-- Ans: Future reference aur auditing ke liye deleted employee ki details store karte hain.

-- Q9. What happens if DELETE affects no rows?
-- Ans: Koi row delete nahi hoti, isliye row-level trigger execute nahi hota.

-- Q10. What is the difference between BEFORE and AFTER triggers?
-- Ans: BEFORE trigger operation se pehle aur AFTER trigger operation ke baad execute hota hai.

-- Q11. What is an audit table?
-- Ans: Audit table important database activities aur changes ka record maintain karti hai.

-- Q12. What is the purpose of COMMIT?
-- Ans: COMMIT transaction ke changes permanently save karta hai.

-- Q13. Can a trigger insert data into another table?
-- Ans: Haan, trigger ke andar INSERT statement use karke doosri table mein data store kar sakte hain.

-- Q14. What happens to :OLD values during DELETE?
-- Ans: :OLD deleted employee ki values available karata hai.

-- Q15. What is the purpose of SHOW ERRORS?
-- Ans: Isse trigger compile karte waqt aayi errors check kar sakte hain.
